.TH CHTTPSVR_SET_ENGINE_MEM_MGMT_PROCS 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttpsvr_set_engine_mem_mgmt_procs \- set custom memory management for engine-level allocations
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <chttpserver.h>

ccol_retval_t chttpsvr_set_engine_mem_mgmt_procs(ccol_memmgmt_procs_t *mp);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Redirects every allocation made by the shared event_loop reactor's own
construction and connection-registration bookkeeping to the
malloc/free/calloc/realloc supplied in mp, exactly like the memory
management procs accepted by every other module in this library.
Passing NULL reverts to the default allocator.

This is independent of the allocator each individual chttpsvr instance
uses for its own connections/requests (configured via
create_chttpsvr_mp, following the usual _mp convention); this function
only affects the one shared reactor's own construction.

This function may only be called before the first chttpsvr_start call
in the process: once the reactor has allocated memory with one set of
procs, swapping to a different malloc/free pairing would corrupt the
heap.  It may be called again after the reactor has fully stopped
(chttpsvr_engine_wait has returned), before the next chttpsvr_start.

If mp is non-NULL, all four function pointers (malloc, free, calloc,
realloc) must be set.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success on success.
ccol_invalid_args if mp is non-NULL but has a NULL function pointer.
ccol_not_permitted if the reactor is already running; stop it first.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpsvr_set_engine_logger (3),
.BR chttpsvr_start (3),
.BR chttpsvr_engine_stop (3),
.BR chttpsvr_engine_wait (3)
